## How to Make Fall Nail Art Last Longer

DIY <strong>fall nail art</strong> typically holds for five to seven days with regular polish and up to two to three weeks with gel, and the biggest factor in that range isn't the design, it's the top coat and the prep underneath it.

Seal every design under a proper top coat, not a quick-dry topper, since quick-dry formulas are thinner and wear down faster over detailed work. Reapply top coat alone every two to three days to extend wear without redoing the art underneath. Nail length matters more than most people expect: shorter nails flex less at the tip during everyday use, which means less cracking along detailed edges. If you're working with a shorter length already, our guide to <a href='/blog/fall/short-fall-nails'>short fall nails</a> covers shapes that hold intricate art particularly well.

Avoid hot water and heavy hand cream directly after finishing; give the top coat a full hour to properly harden before either.

